The store's schema, one revision at a time.

`alembic.ini` is at the repository root and holds three lines; the DSN is not one of
them -- `env.py` reads it through `edge/store/session.py`, so a migration and a running
process address the same database by the same rule.

  uv run alembic upgrade head                  apply every revision to the attached database
  uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "" write the next one from a change to `models.py`

Autogenerate compares the database to `edge/store/models.py`. Read what it wrote before
committing it: it is good at columns and bad at intent.
